       wwaaddddssttrr writes the characters of the (null-terminated)  string  _s_t_r  to
       the  window _w_i_n.  Its process is similar to calling wwaaddddcchh(3X) for each
       _c_h_a_r in _s_t_r.  Control characters are processed as in wwaaddddcchh(3X).

       wwaaddddnnssttrr writes at most _n characters, or until a terminating null char‐
       acter occurs in _s_t_r.  If _n is -1, wwaaddddnnssttrr writes the entire string.

       nnccuurrsseess(3X) describes the variants of these functions.

